data: {"v":{"message":{"id":"3c4500b7-910d-4710-aa1f-e403d6e6c8dd","author":{"role":"tool","name":"web.run","metadata":{"real_author":"tool:web.run"}},"create_time":1793565300.3582733,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"text","parts":[""]},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"search_result_groups":[{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.macworld.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.macworld.com/article/668980/best-magsafe-chargers.html","title":"Best MagSafe and magnetic wireless chargers for iPhone 2026 | Macworld","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":160503,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":0},"pub_date":1784246400.0,"attribution":"www.macworld.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.tomsguide.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-wireless-chargers","title":"The best wireless chargers for iPhone and Android in 2026","snippet":"The article reviews the best wireless chargers for iPhone and Android in 2026, comparing their performance, features, portability, and value. The Belkin BoostCharge Pro 3-in-1 Wireless Charging Pad is the overall winner, offering 15W MagSafe charging for compatible iPhones, Apple Watch charging, and a dedicated space for AirPods. For budget-conscious buyers, the OtterBox Wireless Charging Pad provides reliable 15W universal charging at an affordable price.\n\nOther recommendations include the Satechi 3-in-1 Foldable Qi2 Charging Stand for versatile home and travel use, the compact Anker MagGo 3-in-1 for travelers, and the premium Nomad Stand One for its metal-and-glass construction. The Zens Quattro Charger Pro 4 can charge four devices simultaneously, while Belkin\u2019s UltraCharge Pro adds cooling and supports up to 25W. The InfinaCore P3 Pro combines wireless charging with a 10,000mAh power bank and up to 65W wired output.\n\nWhen choosing a charger, consumers should check device compatibility, charging speeds, included power adapters, and multi-device requirements. Qi is widely supported, while MagSafe offers magnetic charging for iPhones and Qi2 extends similar capabilities to compatible Android phones. Testing involves at least a week of everyday use, overnight charging, timed charging tests, and assessments of design and practicality.","ref_id":{"turn_index":160503,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":12},"pub_date":1778161557.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/pAKH12QqpHgMvkLRWPKzdEnUF42Vftk_3g0qKnV7hVhO6agqH0XZd8Ky-GSELE_jGpS-qPaxK4puMwOEH-IqPLNqMp_79sr5mcagSf_zKleYUnGLxqq5oEWDnsfmUwOX","attribution":"www.tomsguide.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.wired.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.wired.com/gallery/best-wireless-chargers/","title":"Best Wireless Chargers (2026): My Picks After Testing 100+ | WIRED","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":160503,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":1},"pub_date":1786665600.0,"attribution":"www.wired.com"},{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.wired.com/story/mophie-magsafe-3-in-1-wireless-charging-stand-deal","title":"One of My Favorite Apple 3-in-1 Charging Stands Is Half Off Today","snippet":"WIRED highlights the Mophie MagSafe 3-in-1 Charging Stand as a particularly versatile Apple charging accessory, currently available at nearly half price\u201449 percent off, reportedly its lowest price yet. The stand wirelessly charges an iPhone, Apple Watch, and AirPods or other compatible earbuds while reducing desk or nightstand clutter. Its standout feature is an adjustable telescoping pole, allowing the iPhone charging pad to extend from 7.5 to 16 inches and tilt to a preferred angle. This makes it suitable for low nightstands, standing desks, video calls, and content creation. The phone can also be rotated horizontally for Apple\u2019s StandBy mode. The charger is MFi- and Qi-certified, delivering up to 15 watts to an iPhone, 5 watts to an Apple Watch, and 5 watts to earbuds. It includes a 36-watt power adapter and a 5-foot USB-C cable. The article recommends it especially for users who need adjustable phone height, a feature uncommon among competing chargers.","ref_id":{"turn_index":160503,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":15},"pub_date":1789725600.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/w852amh6mi7jMZOY7bX09NVO6Fkkbihs5354dqai43QTHiCwJWII7rPBem2EjxdT9GPMPaYVS41QqF6aqQ-buV8YlTh5eSdoLbT4zBfh65hxEgm6OiRH53SZFx34GO9TVRHbHsOSto3Dg1c5-FZj5P7tjTqXgTVJkpbHnmWivl7U3jFmFiRgSHFYK-U4EyApOXczN2QA5ycGT93EYoeg2KzhDja0ZKYQ3emld12DWvA","attribution":"www.wired.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.techradar.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.techradar.com/best/best-iphone-chargers","title":"I've tested more than 25 USB-C chargers, and these are the best iPhone chargers money can buy","snippet":"TechRadar\u2019s guide evaluates more than 25 iPhone chargers tested over 18 months, judging charging performance, design, versatility, and value. Its overall winner is the UGreen Uno Charger 100W, a four-port USB-C/USB-A charger capable of powering iPhones, MacBooks, and multiple accessories simultaneously. Its distinctive robot-style display and frequent discounts below $50/\u00a345 add to its appeal. Other recommendations include the compact, inexpensive UGreen Nexode Mini 30W for budgets under $20; the UGreen Nexode 65W with a retractable built-in USB-C cable for travel; Anker\u2019s Nano 45W charger with a six-foot cable for a charger-and-cable bundle; the Iniu SnapGo Air 10,000mAh power bank for 45W wired and 25W magnetic wireless charging; and ESR\u2019s Qi2 Mini for affordable 15W wireless charging. The guide emphasizes choosing USB-C, sufficient wattage for future devices, appropriate port numbers, and compatibility with wireless charging speeds. Testing involved timing full charges from zero and assessing multi-port performance using a consistent cable.","ref_id":{"turn_index":160503,"ref_type":